Chris,

There was mention of a lujvo frequency list on lojban list back in 2003:
http://www.lojban.org/he/lists/lojban-list/msg04985.html , but the link
in that message is dead. Perhaps someone has a copy of it somewhere that
they could put up on lojban.org.

That message does list the top 10 from the frequency list, which I am
reproducing here for those who can't be bothered to click through.
However, it doesn't strike me as terribly informative because there is
so much from one source (Alice), plus it includes "jbovlaste", which is
normally used as a cmene.

noltruni'u (queen, from Alice) - 72
xacyce'a (gun, from jbosnu) - 69
noltrunau (king, from Alice) - 66
cakyrespa (turtle, from Alice) - 59
mapypre (hat-person? from Alice) - 57
cpicinfo (bird-lion? from Alice) - 52
selsku (is said, from everywhere) - 47
jbovlaste (Lojban dictionary, from IRC) - 43
cabdei (today, from everywhere) - 42
skudji (mean to say, from IRC) - 41

A rafsi frequency list would also be nice -- perhaps one can be derived
from the lujvo freq list if we can find it.

mu'o mi'e sen



